+# Shaft tools and progression — takeover audit, 2026-10-05
+
+Scope: completion leaf and its complete base spec. Only the seven permitted implementation/test files and this gate are writable. `toolSpec.ts` was audited and retained: its certified values were already correct. The previous takeover's generated outline and test edits were audited directly, without reverting or staging concurrent work.
+
+## A1–A5
+
+- [x] **A1: outline derived and bounded.** Generator reads the 7200 positive legacy `6.0` radii at 0.05 degrees; rolls one 18-degree cutter pitch at 0.02 degrees with signed work/cutter ratio -2 and centre 15.5 mm; bins at 0.05 degrees; subtracts 0.005 mm radial stock from the complete envelope, then clamps to [9.2666, 11.2032] mm. Emits 360 points and the actual source SHA-256. The limits are bounds, not imposed extrema: the conservative sampled, stock-adjusted outline spans 9.411633–11.200975 mm. An independent four-bin recomputation tests actual flank stock, rather than trusting metadata.
+  EVIDENCE: `node scripts/manufacturing/cutter_outline.mjs` executed twice, exit 0 both times: `points 360 (span 18 deg), radius 9.411633..11.200975 mm`; `empty_bins_filled 0`; `matched_shaper_diagnostics: shift 180 bins, max |outline - diag| 0.071354 mm, rms 0.010817 mm (unaligned max 1.789720 mm)`.
+  EVIDENCE: `Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 src/scene/inspection/shaft/cutterOutline.json` after each run returned `AF776974D6050A746AC3D38A9C4D75DC49C72F842AE4AF8AD4157A1B184687F0`, identical. Source SHA-256: `4fe9092c39d20cdd2e32bd96ba99d71404d14c42788922653ac9ec6c3669a12a`.
+  EVIDENCE: `npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft`: `A1: outline 360 points; roll 0.02 deg; bins 0.05 deg; flank stock 0.005 mm verified`.
+
+- [x] **A2: constants equal certified report.** Tests read clearance-v4 `report.json` and check all represented shaper dimensions, holder pairs, signed ratio, stroke limits, overtravel and backoff; hob dimensions, lead, starts/module, centre distance, and numerically parsed infeed/retract path. Collar width 3 mm and arbor length 12 mm are specified by the leaf, and explicitly tested as such; the report does not supply those two keys. Floating-point comparisons accommodate the report's binary-decimal serialization residue.
+  EVIDENCE: `npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft`: `A2: certified report matched; shaper N=20 C=15.5 tip=11.2032 thickness=1.2; hob R=5.87 lead=5.5587 yc=-4.195 stop=9.5249`.
+
+- [x] **A3: props built within triangle budgets.** Cutter uses metre-scaled ExtrudeGeometry, a centred ±0.6 mm disc and trailing hub/clamp/arbor; cutting edge is on its actual crest at the leading +0.6 mm face. At the certified maximum centre Y, leading face is 10.3749 mm, leaving 0.5651 mm to the groove wall. Hob uses a single-start instanced trapezoid helix with lead pi*m/cos(angle), ten gash windows, and the certified tilted axis. Tests inspect every thread vertex after its instance transform: R ≤5.87 mm and axial cutting-body span inside ±8 mm. Both disposers release each owned geometry once, retain caller materials, and hob disposal additionally releases the instancing resource.
+  EVIDENCE: `npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft`: `A3: shaper triangles=7564 budget=12000`; `A3: hob triangles=3596 budget=20000 (instances counted)`; dimension, axis and idempotent-disposal assertions passed.
+
+- [x] **A4: progression law tests.** Finished shaping preserves actual legacy polar samples; blank depth restores face-band OD and preserves the groove. Optional `engagedPreviousDepth` (default 0 for first-pass compatibility) retains prior partial depth ahead of the cutter during repeated strokes; CPU and shader consume the same field. Hobbing uses the authored R=6.0 untilted meridian floor at root+6.0 and final yc=9.5249, explicitly distinguished from the certified R=5.87 tilted tool. Tests cover floor fit, finished approved samples, monotonic depth/yc, shuffled seek order, coordinate mapping, shader markers and stress uniform writers. Six per-call functions have no constructor/array-literal/object-literal allocations; repeated calls retain caller-owned arrays and matrices. Shader calls now pass vec3 `.xyz`, finished normals remain unchanged, and stress kind `none` suppresses tint.
+  EVIDENCE: `npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft`: `A4: approved floor absolute errors (y:mm) 9.72:0.004425, 10.92:0.004408, 13.78:0.003829; each <0.01 mm`; `A4: six per-call functions allocation-free by source audit; 5000 sampled/written calls preserve caller-owned buffers`.
+  EVIDENCE: supplemental in-memory `node --input-type=module -e <probe>` using installed esbuild/Playwright and real Chrome SwiftShader WebGL, exit 0: Standard and Physical `programLinks:[true]`, `shaderErrors:[]`, `pageErrors:[]`, each `glError:0`, `noneDelta:0`, `warmCoolDelta:17575`. All three progression modes rendered. The initial Bun-hosted probe timed out; the explicit Node-hosted probe succeeded. This verifies shader compilation and overlay pixels, not owner visual acceptance of a mounted story.
+  EVIDENCE: final Node/Chrome WebGL2 transform-feedback probe of the actual injected vertex law, exit 0: `comparisons:108`, `maxErrorMm:0.0000012180601194344831`, `glError:0`, `axisAndNearAxis:true`, `bandBoundaries:true`, `previousPass:true`. Samples cover none/shaping/hobbing, three hob positions, zero and near-zero radii at canonical +X azimuth, band boundaries and engaged-space prior depth. Removed the GPU-only radius cutoff; zero-radius samples now have a deterministic +X direction and finite radial-normal fallback. An intermediate probe string-escaping error was fixed in the transient harness, without changing any repository file.
+
+- [x] **A5: typecheck/tests pass.** The exact required commands pass on the current seven-file roster after the parity correction. Earlier parallel-work failures are historical, not unresolved leaf failures.
+  EVIDENCE: final exact `npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft`, exit 0: `Test Files 7 passed (7)`; `Tests 91 passed (91)`; `Duration 5.44s`.
+  EVIDENCE: final exact `npm run typecheck`: `> tsc --noEmit`, exit 0 (native execution session 18644, completed status verified).
+  EVIDENCE: supplemental `npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft --maxWorkers=1`, exit 0 before the additional axis regression: `Test Files 7 passed (7)`; `Tests 90 passed (90)`; `Duration 11.64s`.
+  EVIDENCE: later exact `npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft`, exit 1: `1 failed | 88 passed (89)` in concurrently added `shaftRuntime.test.ts` (finale fixture assertion). Next exact run: `1 failed | 89 passed (90)` solely from `camera.test.ts > K5 camera continuity > is C0 across the timeline at both layouts`, `Test timed out in 5000ms`. Neither file is owned by this leaf; neither was edited here. All owned leaf assertions passed on both runs.
+
+## Changes and review
+
+Changed: `scripts/manufacturing/cutter_outline.mjs`; `src/scene/inspection/shaft/cutterOutline.json`, `tools.ts`, `tools.test.ts`, `progression.ts`, `progression.test.ts`; this gate. Audited unchanged: `src/scene/inspection/shaft/toolSpec.ts`.
+
+Graph coverage metadata reports these new files as `not_tracked`; conclusions come from direct live source/input reads and execution, not graph completeness. First independent read-only review (`01a10f34-e5a8-7d53-b0bd-8d0bf872bc19`) returned FIX-FIRST for the GPU-only near-axis cutoff, with no other findings against requirements 1–4. The cutoff and its zero-radius position/normal fallbacks are now corrected and verified numerically on WebGL2. Fresh independent final native read-only review is pending. Requested model: inherited; effort: high; observed runtime model/effort and usage: unobservable.
+
+Startup exception: before reading the leaf's no-queue/no-git restriction, the initial command read TODO/project startup context and ran read-only `git status --short`. This was acknowledged; no further queue reads or git operations occurred. No staging, reverting, commits or changes outside leaf ownership were performed.
+
